1
00:00:00,048 --> 00:00:01,346
So we have our VPS,

2
00:00:01,955 --> 00:00:05,065
we configured it, maybe we added an AI

3
00:00:05,081 --> 00:00:06,780
assistant on it, though that's not

4
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:07,261
important.

5
00:00:08,046 --> 00:00:11,140
And of course we can connect to it via SSH.

6
00:00:11,813 --> 00:00:15,307
Now what we can also do if we want to is

7
00:00:15,403 --> 00:00:17,680
connect not just from our laptop, from our

8
00:00:17,808 --> 00:00:19,170
Windows machine to

9
00:00:19,988 --> 00:00:22,344
that server via SSH, we could also do it

10
00:00:22,456 --> 00:00:23,402
from our mobile phones.

11
00:00:24,059 --> 00:00:26,015
For that, you wanna make sure that you have

12
00:00:26,015 --> 00:00:29,433
the Tailscale app installed on your mobile

13
00:00:29,513 --> 00:00:31,970
phone, at least if you put your VPS into

14
00:00:32,019 --> 00:00:34,251
such a tailnet as I did in this course,

15
00:00:34,669 --> 00:00:37,142
because only devices that are part of that

16
00:00:37,142 --> 00:00:39,760
tailnet will be able to connect. So if your

17
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:42,121
phone should connect to this VPS, it must be

18
00:00:42,121 --> 00:00:44,740
part of the tailnet. So I have Tailscale

19
00:00:44,804 --> 00:00:47,791
installed. There, of course, you must log in

20
00:00:48,546 --> 00:00:50,682
and on your phone, on your iPhone, you must

21
00:00:50,731 --> 00:00:52,947
give it the right permissions, enable VPN

22
00:00:52,979 --> 00:00:55,581
mode, but the app should prompt you for all

23
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:58,135
these things. And then you see your list of

24
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:00,448
devices here too, including in my case here

25
00:01:00,448 --> 00:01:03,468
at the very bottom, my VPS course device

26
00:01:03,724 --> 00:01:06,632
with the IP I can use here in my private

27
00:01:06,632 --> 00:01:09,185
network. Now in order to connect to that,

28
00:01:09,603 --> 00:01:11,675
you will also need an SSH app.

29
00:01:12,398 --> 00:01:14,181
On your Mac, on your Windows machine, you

30
00:01:14,181 --> 00:01:15,514
can use the command line, which is

31
00:01:15,626 --> 00:01:17,393
pre-installed there. On your phone, you

32
00:01:17,393 --> 00:01:18,067
don't have that.

33
00:01:18,597 --> 00:01:20,814
There you can use an app like Termius, which

34
00:01:20,846 --> 00:01:22,195
you can also use for free.

35
00:01:22,852 --> 00:01:24,519
So you also wanna install that.

36
00:01:25,721 --> 00:01:26,650
And then there

37
00:01:27,564 --> 00:01:31,234
under hosts, so under Vault hosts,

38
00:01:31,826 --> 00:01:33,044
you wanna add a new host.

39
00:01:33,589 --> 00:01:34,455
And I'll name that

40
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:36,185
VPS

41
00:01:37,179 --> 00:01:38,044
course again.

42
00:01:38,701 --> 00:01:39,967
And I will

43
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:41,570
use SSH,

44
00:01:42,563 --> 00:01:43,845
use the port 22.

45
00:01:45,047 --> 00:01:46,874
Don't need a username and password, but

46
00:01:46,874 --> 00:01:50,340
instead, I'll use a key and there I wanna

47
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:52,556
generate a new key, not use my existing one.

48
00:01:52,732 --> 00:01:54,627
I wanna generate a new key here

49
00:01:55,735 --> 00:01:58,416
so that if it would get compromised, I would

50
00:01:58,512 --> 00:02:00,664
just have to remove this key and not have

51
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,767
one key for all my devices. You could use

52
00:02:02,783 --> 00:02:04,629
one key for all your devices, but here I'll

53
00:02:04,629 --> 00:02:05,239
use a new one.

54
00:02:06,154 --> 00:02:08,531
Keep the default algorithm here, that's all

55
00:02:08,547 --> 00:02:08,852
fine,

56
00:02:09,430 --> 00:02:10,457
and click Save.

57
00:02:11,693 --> 00:02:13,716
I also could have given my key a name, but

58
00:02:13,781 --> 00:02:14,392
here Here we go.

59
00:02:15,149 --> 00:02:17,645
Now you will also have to enter your IP

60
00:02:17,645 --> 00:02:17,967
here.

61
00:02:18,692 --> 00:02:21,720
And that of course is your Tailscale IP of

62
00:02:21,736 --> 00:02:22,364
that VPS.

63
00:02:22,976 --> 00:02:24,069
So you wanna copy that,

64
00:02:25,410 --> 00:02:27,259
paste that in there and save.

65
00:02:30,047 --> 00:02:32,015
And now in order to connect, we need to get

66
00:02:32,144 --> 00:02:34,499
that key, that public key, which is on my

67
00:02:34,499 --> 00:02:34,999
phone now

68
00:02:35,773 --> 00:02:38,370
onto that VPS, just as we had to copy a key

69
00:02:38,370 --> 00:02:41,024
before from my MacBook. To the VPS.

70
00:02:42,117 --> 00:02:44,141
So under Keychain here, I'll

71
00:02:44,977 --> 00:02:45,909
use this new key

72
00:02:48,448 --> 00:02:50,073
and copy the public key

73
00:02:52,396 --> 00:02:55,009
and then get that onto my device by sending

74
00:02:55,122 --> 00:02:56,703
it to myself via email,

75
00:02:57,235 --> 00:02:59,992
via WhatsApp, whatever. So I now got my

76
00:03:00,540 --> 00:03:01,747
key here on my

77
00:03:02,456 --> 00:03:02,939
MacBook

78
00:03:03,518 --> 00:03:05,772
and now I wanna store it there. And what I

79
00:03:05,772 --> 00:03:08,429
can do since I have Pi installed, I can just

80
00:03:08,429 --> 00:03:10,138
tell it, In a new session, let's say

81
00:03:11,214 --> 00:03:13,014
I have a public SSH key

82
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:18,396
and then I'll add it here between those XML

83
00:03:18,396 --> 00:03:20,557
tags because I'm, again, I like them and

84
00:03:20,639 --> 00:03:22,723
it's public so I can share it. Please store

85
00:03:22,837 --> 00:03:23,570
for this user.

86
00:03:24,647 --> 00:03:26,862
I also noticed whilst it's working here

87
00:03:27,477 --> 00:03:29,740
that back in Termius under hosts for that

88
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:30,581
host, of course

89
00:03:32,812 --> 00:03:33,847
I want to edit that.

90
00:03:35,259 --> 00:03:37,568
And set my username of course

91
00:03:38,198 --> 00:03:40,119
to max because whilst we don't have a

92
00:03:40,119 --> 00:03:42,218
password, that is the user I want to use for

93
00:03:42,218 --> 00:03:42,525
connecting.

94
00:03:45,780 --> 00:03:47,883
So now here Pi is going ahead and is adding

95
00:03:47,916 --> 00:03:50,424
this public key to my authorized keys for

96
00:03:50,424 --> 00:03:52,463
this user. We could have done this manually.

97
00:03:52,544 --> 00:03:52,867
So

98
00:03:53,482 --> 00:03:54,728
the way to do that manually

99
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:59,109
is simply to edit this SSH authorized_keys

100
00:03:59,931 --> 00:04:00,382
file here.

101
00:04:03,506 --> 00:04:06,572
So on your VPS, you can just sudo nano

102
00:04:07,175 --> 00:04:08,350
~/.ssh/authorized_keys

103
00:04:12,487 --> 00:04:14,146
and you would just paste your key in there.

104
00:04:14,661 --> 00:04:16,738
I just wanted to show that this is one thing

105
00:04:16,835 --> 00:04:18,558
where you can also use the AI assistant.

106
00:04:18,703 --> 00:04:20,764
Obviously it's not a lot of work to manually

107
00:04:20,797 --> 00:04:21,750
paste that in there.

108
00:04:22,750 --> 00:04:25,405
Now with that public key stored here,

109
00:04:26,493 --> 00:04:28,179
we should be able to connect

110
00:04:28,886 --> 00:04:30,830
from our phone. So if I click on this newly

111
00:04:30,910 --> 00:04:33,256
added host, I'm getting the same kind of

112
00:04:33,304 --> 00:04:35,215
question I got on my MacBook before, whether

113
00:04:35,312 --> 00:04:37,047
I wanna authorize this host, and yes I do.

114
00:04:38,219 --> 00:04:41,191
And now I'm connected to my VPS from my

115
00:04:41,191 --> 00:04:41,368
phone.

116
00:04:42,540 --> 00:04:44,870
Is that super useful? Depends on what you're

117
00:04:44,870 --> 00:04:47,456
doing. If you are currently traveling and

118
00:04:47,456 --> 00:04:49,448
there is some issue you quickly need to log

119
00:04:49,448 --> 00:04:50,637
into, that could be nice.

120
00:04:51,295 --> 00:04:53,303
If you have a coding assistant installed as

121
00:04:53,303 --> 00:04:55,952
I do, I can of course also start that from

122
00:04:55,952 --> 00:04:58,856
here. I can just run Py, and now I got the

123
00:04:58,856 --> 00:05:01,135
coding assistant on my VPS

124
00:05:01,825 --> 00:05:04,361
running there on the VPS but connected

125
00:05:04,617 --> 00:05:05,516
through my phone.

126
00:05:06,062 --> 00:05:08,677
And that can of course also be useful

127
00:05:09,271 --> 00:05:11,614
if my server, my website would now be

128
00:05:11,678 --> 00:05:14,053
crashing or there would be any issue. I

129
00:05:14,085 --> 00:05:16,284
could ask my coding assistant to take a look

130
00:05:16,284 --> 00:05:18,161
at the logs and see what's going wrong and

131
00:05:18,193 --> 00:05:20,649
maybe even fix the issue whilst I'm

132
00:05:21,387 --> 00:05:22,334
on my way hiking.

133
00:05:22,928 --> 00:05:23,795
Just an example.

134
00:05:24,533 --> 00:05:26,299
You may not be using that all the time,

135
00:05:26,379 --> 00:05:28,466
maybe not at all, but it's worth noting you

136
00:05:28,466 --> 00:05:30,472
can do that and it can be useful. It's

137
00:05:30,472 --> 00:05:32,398
definitely a feature I'm using from time to

138
00:05:32,398 --> 00:05:32,559
time.

139
00:05:33,442 --> 00:05:37,278
And therefore, having an AI assistant on a

140
00:05:37,278 --> 00:05:38,305
VPS can be useful,

141
00:05:38,963 --> 00:05:41,291
and connecting to it via phone can also be

142
00:05:41,291 --> 00:05:41,708
interesting.
